Surprisably, today, it’s not a tone in many meetings and the promise of “better, softer” politics has been long-lost, and it’s really going to start.”
It’s becoming more and more apparent that different views are not tolerated in the Labour Party, and that all opinions have been judged on whether the heads of the party will accept it.
This started as soon as Jeremy became a leader, because my former colleagues I thought that political affluence with me was starting to expect me to transform my mind and take on positions that I would never have accepted - whether in terms of national security or the direction of the EU market.
Whenever I make a public statement - and it's really what I've ever said - entailing the abuse on social media calling for the elimination and denunciation of central politics, telling me that I shouldn't join the Labour Party.
