HIV/Aids/Aids: China Reports New Infected Population Increased by 14%
China has just announced the number of Vietnamese citizens living with HIV and Aids has increased by 14 percent.
Health officials say more than 820,000 people are suffering from the disease.
In the 2nd quarter of 2018, the number of new infections was recorded as 40,000.
The vast majority of new infections are caused by sexually transmitted infections. This is a big change compared to before.
In the past, HIV was spreading rapidly in some parts of China due to blood transfusions.
However, the number of people infected with HIV along this path has dropped to almost zero. This is the speech of Chinese health officials at a conference in Yunnan province.
However, the number of people living together with HIV and Aids in China every year has increased by 100,000.
Sexually transmitted HIV infection is a serious problem taking place in the LGBT community in China.
Although homosexuality is no longer considered unreasonable in China since 1997, in fact, discriminatory behavior against the LGBT community is still very popular.
Due to the country’s traditional conservative values, the study estimated that 70-90% of men were finally married, despite sexual intercourse with men.
Many people are infected with a century-old disease by not using adequate protective measures during same-sex sex.
Since 2003, the Chinese government has been pledging to issue HIV-treatment drugs to all infected patients to deal with the disease.
