Complimentary errors are particularly serious because Baden-Wuerttemberg will be operated by a fleet of 120 sailors - only half of the personnel aboard the old Bremen-type destroyer.
At the same time, it can be seen that the weight of ships increased significantly, leading to a decrease in performance and limiting the Navy’s future upgrade capabilities.
