“This is a unique product,” someone else commented.
“It’s an interesting ad aimed at mothers who need to pump milk (often at work or in the toilets) and they feel they’re like “bukes”.
“This isn’’t an advertisement that praises the dairy industry.”
At the end of the video, a group of women revealed that they had danced with a milk suction machine that had been concealed in their undershirts.
The idea behind this campaign is based on the fact that many women who pump milk to lactate say that they feel they look like cows.
However, the Elvie pump does not cause noise, no wires or tubes and is neatly inside the breastfeeding bra, helping women to be able to move freely, hold the baby and even go out while pumping milk.
Ana Balarin, ECD and ECD at Mother commented: "The Elvie pump is really a revolutionary product, worthy of a daring introduction and encouraging incitement.
When comparing women to dairy cows, we want people to be aware of breast-supply products and related challenges, while expressing a hilarious and sympathetical way about the freedom the new suction product brings to mothers.
